sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Morphotype 1 Anthrobots are likely non-movers or stationary wigglers, which the authors suggest may be because their radially symmetric spherical shape with evenly distributed cilia makes ciliary propulsion forces cancel out, with small imbalances producing only wiggling.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Spherical bots with uniform cilia may not move because ciliary forces cancel";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Gumuskaya G, Srivastava P, Cooper BG, Lesser H, Semegran B, Garnier S, Levin M, “Motile Living Biobots Self-Construct from Adult Human Somatic Progenitor Seed Cells”, Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany) (2024), doi:10.1002/advs.202303575; section “Results › Distinct Movement Types and Morphotypes are Highly Correlated”. Scope: Small, spherical, uniformly ciliated Anthrobots (morphotype 1)"
}
